.TH WB\-INIT 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-init \- set Watchbill up in this repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR init [\-\-yes]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Set Watchbill up in the git repository of this folder: propose what the repository says about itself (its name, the git server of origin, a folder of requirements, the CI driver), ask one line per answer, show the file and write .watchbill/watchbill.yml at the root of the repository. \-\-yes (\-y) takes what it found and asks nothing. A file that is already there is never changed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Take what it found and ask nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file is written.
.TP
.B 1
It was refused.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
.BR wb\-check (1) ,
.BR wb\-upgrade (1)
